  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 22 files needed to plan this cross-repo refactor, ordered by centrality to the threading-model change:\n\n**spring-kafka (primary implementation, 12 files)** \u2014 `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer`, `KafkaMessageListenerContainer`, and `AbstractMessageListenerContainer` (the core class hierarchy being refactored); `MessageListenerContainer` and `ContainerProperties` (contracts/config it must preserve); `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory`/`AbstractKafkaListenerContainerFactory`/`KafkaListenerContainerFactory` (factory layer that wires concurrency into containers); `KafkaListenerEndpointRegistry`/`KafkaListenerEndpoint`/`MethodKafkaListenerEndpoint` (lifecycle management of created containers); `KafkaListener` annotation (exposes the `concurrency` attribute at the API surface).\n\n**spring-boot (autoconfiguration consumer, 4 files)** \u2014 `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactoryConfigurer` and `KafkaProperties` (bind/apply concurrency settings), `KafkaAutoConfiguration` and `KafkaAnnotationDrivenConfiguration` (wire the factory bean into Spring context).\n\n**spring-framework (core abstractions, 5 files)** \u2014 `SmartLifecycle`/`Lifecycle`/`LifecycleProcessor` (container start/stop contract implemented by both listener container types) and `TaskExecutor`/`SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor` (the threading abstraction concurrency is built on).\n\nPlus `kafka.adoc` docs, which already document the current concurrency semantics/breaking-change history and are directly useful for drafting the risk/compatibility sections of the plan.",
